invariant: INV-16
file: poly1305.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh poly1305-avx2
reason: the AVX2 update hands the kernel whole groups of four blocks, the
  128-bit path's group, where the kernel takes groups of eight, so an
  update whose whole blocks end inside a group of eight breaks the
  kernel's contract and its CH_ASSERT. Only an x86-64 object compiles the
  line, so the script builds bin/poly1305_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs
  it under qemu-x86_64.

--- old
        size_t grouped = n - n % POLY1305_AVX2_GROUP;
--- new
        size_t grouped = n - n % POLY1305_VECTOR_GROUP;
